  // Outbox TTL for user-facing messages (text, attachments, stickers, and
  // their no-device retry queue). Set to 7 DAYS (2026-07-13, up from 24 h) so a
  // message survives a long offline stretch — overnight + a workday, travel, a
  // dead/charging phone — instead of silently expiring from the local outbox or
  // the relay mailbox. Reliable delivery is the product's #1 requirement. This
  // matches the relay's own mailbox retention cap
  // (SECRETLY_RELAY_MAX_TTL_SECONDS = 7 days), so the relay honours the full
  // window (it clamps min(requested, cap) = 7d). Group content rides this same
  // TTL via sendControlMessage's group-envelope promotion.
  // Control-plane messages (call signals, session-reset pings,
  // peer-history requests) intentionally keep the original short TTL
  // because they are meaningless to redeliver days later.
  // See docs/MESSAGE_DELIVERY_AUDIT_2026-05-28.md §10.2 C5 and
  // docs/DELIVERY_AUDIT_2026-07-13.md (F1, ASK-1).
  static const int _outboxUserMessageTtlSeconds = 7 * 24 * 60 * 60;

