  int _foregroundSinceMs = 0;
  // In-app banner is for messages that arrive WHILE you're using the app. A
  // message caught up from the backlog is not "live": suppress its banner if it
  // landed inside the post-resume grace, or if the message itself is older than
  // the live window (belt-and-suspenders for a slow drain). Neither gate touches
  // the background/system push — only the foreground banner.
  // 2026-07-19 (user report: "native notification already came, then I open
  // the app and the SAME messages banner again one by one"): 4 s only covered
  // the first drain tick — a deep-sleep backlog keeps applying for 10-20 s
  // after resume (fetch + per-wire decrypt), and everything applied in that
  // window already produced a system notification while the app was asleep.
  // 20 s covers the realistic catch-up; a genuinely NEW message during those
