  bool get inboundFirstDrainDone => _relay?.firstDrainCompleted ?? false;

  // HTTP reachability of the relay, tracked SEPARATELY from the WS. The WS can
  // fail to reach "ready" within the 6s budget on MIUI / slow links while plain
  // HTTP (the inbox pump + call signalling) still works — so a WS failure must
  // never surface a "Relay is offline" banner on its own. Set by HTTP health
  // probes; gates the banner clear so it can't latch while messaging works.
  bool _relayHttpReachable = false;
  // Room HTTP mutations (settings, profile, members, invite-links, etc.) call
  // the relay HTTP API directly and do not depend on the WebSocket session, so
  // gating them on `_relayOnline` (a WS-only health signal) blocks legitimate
  // operations whenever the WS link blips during a network change. Only
  // `_transportBlocked` (set when the user has explicitly blocked traffic, or
  // protocol-incompatible relay was detected) should hard-block HTTP work.
  bool get _useAuthoritativeRoomRelay => _relay != null && !_transportBlocked;
  bool _allowLocalRoomFallbackForTesting = false;

